{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "d53adae7-b5f0-4157-9710-4683a44d5601"/*APC40Mk1FeedbackExample*/,
  "Description": "## APC40 Mk1 Feedback Example\n\nThis graph demonstrates encoder-ring feedback and three clip-launch button states with an APC40 Mk1. Connect the APC40 input and output, then use Generic mode for the graph’s MIDI examples.\n\n## Select a mode\n\n- **Shift + Record Arm 1 — Generic (`0x40`)**: use this mode to pass the graph’s MIDI buttons through.\n- **Shift + Record Arm 2 — Ableton Live (`0x41`)**.\n- **Shift + Record Arm 3 — Preset/Snapshot (`0x42`)**: the compatible-device handler consumes its snapshot controls.\n\nWhen TiXL detects matching `Akai APC40` input and output ports, its built-in compatible-device handler sends the introduction SysEx. The graph does not send SysEx, and no separate SysEx checkbox is required.\n\n## Encoder-ring feedback\n\nThe first three Track Control knobs send their value back on the same CC and set the ring type separately:\n\n- **Knob 1:** input/output CC 48; ring-style CC 56 with value 1 (Single).\n- **Knob 2:** input/output CC 49; ring-style CC 57 with value 2 (Volume).\n- **Knob 3:** input/output CC 50; ring-style CC 58 with value 3 (Pan).\n- **Cue Level:** CC 47 uses relative steps. It has no absolute position to reflect as an encoder ring.\n\n## Button feedback\n\nEach example listens for Notes on channel 1 and sends feedback to its matching APC40 clip-launch button:\n\n- **Trigger — Clip Launch 1, note 53:** `MidiInput.WasHit` pulses; `Notes_FixedDuration` lights the button briefly. Green, velocity 1.\n- **Toggle — Clip Launch 2, note 54:** each press increments `CountInt`; `IsIntEven` alternates the light. Yellow, velocity 5. It starts off (`CountInt.DefaultValue = 1`).\n- **Hold — Clip Launch 3, note 55:** `MidiInput.Result > 0.5` stays true while pressed; `Note_WhileTriggered` turns the LED off on release. Red, velocity 3.\n\nAll feedback outputs use channel 1 and device `Akai APC40`. For clip-launch LEDs, velocity 0 is off, 1/2 are green steady/blink, 3/4 are red steady/blink, and 5/6 are yellow steady/blink. Other APC40 buttons may use different LED rules.\n\n## References\n\nSee the [Akai APC40 Communications Protocol, Revision 1](https://cdn.inmusicbrands.com/akai/apc40/APC40_Communications_Protocol_rev_1.pdf_1db97c1fdba23bacf47df0f9bf64e913.pdf) for the Mk1 modes, note mapping, and LED velocities.",
  "InputUis": [],
