    {
      "Id": "aa3caf0d-71e6-4bfe-a2bc-4bbdf7773a88",
      "Title": "Button feedback patterns\n\nEach input listens for Notes on channel 1. Its output sends feedback to\nthe same clip-launch note. All three rows route through a Group into the\nscene's Execute operator.\n\n- Trigger — green, velocity 1: MidiInput.WasHit makes a short pulse;\nNotes_FixedDuration lights Clip Launch 1 (note 53) briefly.\n- Toggle — yellow, velocity 5: WasHit increments CountInt modulo 2;\nIsIntEven keeps Clip Launch 2 (note 54) lit every other press.\n- Hold — red, velocity 3: MidiInput.Result > 0.5 stays true while\npressed; Note_WhileTriggered turns Clip Launch 3 (note 55) off on\nrelease.\n\nAll outputs use channel 1 and device Akai APC40. The toggle starts off\n(CountInt.DefaultValue = 1): the first press turns it on, and the second\nturns it off. The hold example uses the input level because WasHit is\nonly a press pulse.\n\nFor APC40 Mk1 clip-launch LEDs, velocity 0 is off, 1 is green, 2 is\ngreen blink, 3 is red, 4 is red blink, 5 is yellow, and 6 is yellow\nblink. These values apply to the clip-launch LEDs; other APC40 buttons\nmay use different LED rules.",
      "Label": "Readme - Button feedback",
      "Color": {
        "X": 0.6,
        "Y": 0.6,
        "Z": 0.6,
        "W": 1.0
      },
      "Position": {
        "X": 1100.0,
        "Y": 934.0
      },
      "Size": {
        "X": 900.0,
        "Y": 650.0
      }
    },
    {
      "Id": "b45772b6-a69a-4cb2-a3f1-44e7f200af10",
      "Title": "TOGGLE | alternate on/off | clip LED yellow",
